{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793607318,"nonce":"SJpZPJWExOTuZIYiyrZy+Kgm8Yk=","message":"Changed after the 2026-11-02 document review (design §11 and §12 updated to match).\n\nScope additions:\n\n- `omega` decides linear arithmetic over `Int`/`Nat`, but translated C# is over `Int32`/`Int64` (D7). The semantics library gains `Int32`/`Int64` → `Int` bridging lemmas with range side conditions (design §6.2, as `bv_omega` does), and a simp set that rewrites translated arithmetic into omega's fragment. That simp set is tagged in the attribute sidecar.\n- MSBuild hosting: Visual Studio's MSBuild runs on .NET Framework, so a task cannot load the net10.0 engine in-process (D8). `LeanSharp.Build` (netstandard2.0) extracts VIR, writes it in the canonical encoding, and runs `leansharp verify` (net10.0, engine in-process) as a child process via `ToolTask`, mapping its output to MSBuild diagnostics. M5b replaces the child process with the server.\n- Q8 (fuel and time budgets) and Q9 (CI trust policy) are decided when M5a starts. In-process `leansharp verify` enforces the per-unit fuel and wall-clock limits until M5b's server takes over.\n\nExit criterion, made concrete:\n\n- `Increment(x) \u003e x` over `int` fails the build, with its goal shown, under both `dotnet build` and Visual Studio's MSBuild.\n- §5.1's `ValidImpliesPositive` (with `int` in place of `decimal`) passes.\n- One well-founded recursive method whose decrease obligation needs `omega` passes.\n- At least one quantified theorem over a translated `int` method is closed by `simp` then `omega`.\n- The certificate of a verified C# theorem passes the cross-check step for translated output that M4 adds.\n\nCheckpoints, in order:\n\n1. Meta core: metavariable context, whnf/infer through the kernel, unifier, goal pretty-printer.\n2. End-to-end skeleton: a false theorem fails the MSBuild task with its goal shown, using only `intro`/`exact`/`apply`.\n3. `cases`/`induction`, and well-founded recursion with `Spec.Decreases`.\n4. Attribute sidecar export and `simp`.\n5. Bridging lemmas and `omega`.\n6. Exit corpus and the certificate cross-check.","files":null}]}